<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87057" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόδῐκ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>judged first,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκα π.</span> a cause <i>which has
				priority of hearing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				9(1).334.32
			</span></i>(
				Locr.
			, <span class="entity">v B.C.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Michel</u>
				497.2
			</span></i>(Aerae, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Act.
			,<i>judging in first instance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Schwyzer</u>
					328a
				</span></i>
			ii<i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				8
			</span></i>(Delph., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				5040.63
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Crete</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>decided by arbitration,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐθέλω δίκην δοῦναι πρόδικον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					267
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵνα ἀπολάβῃς τὴν τιμὴν τοῦ βάρδου
					πρόδικον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					276.12
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">ii/iii A.D.</span>, cf. ii <i><span class="en">
				p.355
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst., <i>defender, avenger,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				450
			</span></i>(lyr.); <i>representative in legal proceedings, advocate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναικὸς ἑαυτοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					969.7
				</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; esp. of <i>public advocates,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				9(1).694.114
			</span></i>(Corc.): metaph., <i>advocate, patron,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ἐναργείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1083c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> at Sparta, a
			young king's <i>guardian,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.2.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				3
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
